      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.89,
      "end_seconds": 84.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "it's mild honestly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.12,
      "end_seconds": 92.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.41,
      "end_seconds": 97.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "It usually comes with deep fast breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.39,
      "end_seconds": 102.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "okay, what about tummy pain, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.02,
      "end_seconds": 112.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "yes, about the same, about a month. The deep fast breathing? That's been since last Tuesday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.42,
      "end_seconds": 118.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Have you had vomiting before, or is this the the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.31,
      "end_seconds": 127.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Yes something like this happened last year and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.26,
      "end_seconds": 138.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "a few quick ones: cough or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.97,
      "end_seconds": 143.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "hmm, no, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.97,
      "end_seconds": 148.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.45,
      "end_seconds": 152.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "yeah, no, that's all normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.04,
      "end_seconds": 156.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "is your urine normal no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.97,
      "end_seconds": 161.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.74,
      "end_seconds": 166.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.57,
      "end_seconds": 171.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Grass pollen. I come out in... well, sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.35,
      "end_seconds": 190.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
